{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1c4cce9-db7a-4a4d-a4ca-56d643bfa547",
    "name": "fleet-management",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "25603811",
    "description": "Full API collection for the Aivacol Fleet Management backend (brands, models, vehicles, auth).\n\nSetup:\n1. Set the collection variable `baseURL` (e.g. `http://localhost:3000`).\n2. Run `auth > Login` with the seeded user (`aivacol` / `aivacol`) and copy `access_token`/`refresh_token` into the `token`/`refresh_token` variables.\n3. All other requests attach `{{token}}` as a Bearer token automatically.\n4. After creating a brand/model/vehicle, copy the returned `id` into `brand_id`/`model_id`/`vehicle_id` to use it in the following requests."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "brands",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Lists all active brands (soft-deleted ones are excluded).\n\nHow to use: just send it — requires only a valid Bearer `{{token}}}`, no params or body.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with an array of brands (`id`, `name`, `active`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `createdBy`, `updatedBy`). Result is served from the Redis cache (`brands:all`) when available.",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/brands",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "brands"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get by Id",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Fetches a single brand by id.\n\nHow to use: replace the `1` in the URL with the id you want (or run `Create` first and use `{{brand_id}}`).\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with the brand object, or `404 Not Found` if the id doesn't exist or was soft-deleted. Cached in Redis (`brands:{id}`).",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/brands/1",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "brands",
                "1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Creates a new brand.\n\nHow to use: send `{ \"name\": string }` in the body. `created_by` is filled automatically from the JWT (`req.user.nickname`) — no need to send it.\n\nWhat to expect: `201 Created` with the new brand, including its generated `id`. Copy that `id` into the collection variable `brand_id` so the `Update`/`Delete` requests below can use it. Invalidates the `brands:all` cache.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"GWM\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/brands",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "brands"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PUT",
            "description": "Updates an existing brand's name.\n\nHow to use: set the collection variable `brand_id` first (copy it from the `Create` response). Send `{ \"name\": string }` in the body.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with the updated brand, or `404 Not Found` if `brand_id` doesn't exist. `updated_by` is set from the JWT. Invalidates both `brands:all` and `brands:{id}` caches.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"GWM2\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/brands/{{brand_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "brands",
                "{{brand_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "description": "Soft-deletes a brand — sets `active = false` and `updated_by`; the row is never physically removed.\n\nHow to use: make sure `brand_id` is set (see `Create`/`Update`).\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` on success, or `404 Not Found` if the id doesn't exist. The brand disappears from subsequent `Get`/`Get by Id` calls. Invalidates the brand caches.",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/brands/{{brand_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "brands",
                "{{brand_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
