            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Fetches a single vehicle by id, with its `model` (and the model's `brand`) eagerly loaded.\n\nHow to use: set the collection variable `vehicle_id` (see `Create`), it's used in the URL automatically.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with the vehicle plus nested `model`/`brand`, or `404 Not Found` if it doesn't exist or is inactive. Cached in Redis (`vehicles:{id}`).",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles/{{vehicle_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles",
                "{{vehicle_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Registers a new vehicle.\n\nHow to use: send `modelId`, `licensePlate`, `chassis`, `renavam` and `year` in the body — all required, and `licensePlate`/`chassis`/`renavam` must be unique.\n\nWhat to expect: `201 Created` with the new vehicle, `status` defaulted to `disponivel`, and an initial row written to the status-history log. An audit event (`fleet.audit`) is emitted. Copy the returned `id` into the collection variable `vehicle_id` for the requests below.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"modelId\": 1,\n    \"licensePlate\": \"asdafsdf\",\n    \"chassis\": \"32A1SD8CASED0CASDC54231\",\n    \"renavam\": \"3212312313132132\",\n    \"year\": \"2026\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PUT",
            "description": "Updates a vehicle's data (plate, chassis, renavam, year, model). Does **not** change `status` — use `Update Status` below for that.\n\nHow to use: set `vehicle_id` first, then send only the fields you want to change in the body.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with the updated vehicle, or `404 Not Found` if `vehicle_id` doesn't exist. `updated_by` is set from the JWT.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"licensePlate\": \"asdafsdf\",\n    \"chassis\": \"32A1SD8CASED0CASDC54231\",\n    \"renavam\": \"9899999999999999\",\n    \"year\": \"2026\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles/{{vehicle_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles",
                "{{vehicle_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "description": "Soft-deletes a vehicle: sets `active = false`, forces `status = 'inativo'`, and writes a row to the status-history log.\n\nHow to use: make sure `vehicle_id` is set.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` on success, or `404 Not Found` if the id doesn't exist. The vehicle disappears from subsequent list/detail calls but its history is preserved.",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles/{{vehicle_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles",
                "{{vehicle_id}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Status History",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Returns the full status-transition history of a vehicle.\n\nHow to use: set `vehicle_id`; no body needed.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with an array ordered by `changed_at DESC`, each entry containing `from_status`, `to_status`, `changed_by`, `changed_at` and an optional `notes`.",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles/{{vehicle_id}}/status-history",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles",
                "{{vehicle_id}}",
                "status-history"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "description": "Lists all active vehicles.\n\nHow to use: just send it — requires only a valid Bearer token.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with an array of vehicles, each including its nested `model`/`brand`. Served from the Redis cache (`vehicles:all`) when available.",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "description": "Transitions a vehicle to a new operational status.\n\nHow to use: set `vehicle_id`; send `{ \"status\": \"disponivel\" | \"alugado\" | \"manutencao\" | \"inativo\", \"notes\"?: string }` in the body. `notes` is optional (max 500 chars).\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with the updated vehicle, plus a new row written to the status-history log and a `fleet.audit` event emitted. Returns `400 Bad Request` if the requested status is the same as the current one.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"status\": \"manutencao\",\n    \"notes\": \"fasdfasdfdsdcsdcdcsdcsdcsdcsdf\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/vehicles/{{vehicle_id}}/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "vehicles",
                "{{vehicle_id}}",
                "status"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
