    {
      "name": "auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Authenticates a user and issues tokens.\n\nHow to use: send `{ \"login\": string, \"password\": string }` — `login` accepts either the nickname or the email (seeded user: `aivacol` / `aivacol`).\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with `access_token` (valid 15 min) and `refresh_token` (valid 7 days). Copy `access_token` into the collection variable `token` and `refresh_token` into `refresh_token` — every other request in this collection depends on `token` being set.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"login\": \"aivacol\",\n    \"password\": \"aivacol\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Forgot Password",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Starts the password-reset flow for a given email.\n\nHow to use: send `{ \"email\": string }`.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` regardless of whether the email exists (avoids user enumeration). If it exists, a reset token (UUID, 1h TTL) is generated and logged to the **backend console** (no real email is sent) — copy it from there to use in `Reset Password`.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"aivacol@aivacol.com\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/auth/forgot-password",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "forgot-password"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset Password",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Completes the password-reset flow.\n\nHow to use: send `{ \"token\": string, \"password\": string }` — `token` is the UUID printed to the backend console by `Forgot Password`, `password` must be at least 6 characters.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` on success (password hash updated). `400`/`401` if the token is invalid, already used, or expired.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"token\": \"c0541ea6-d3a9-410f-b216-77e4a200ea45\",\n    \"password\": \"Commandos!123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/auth/reset-password",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "reset-password"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Exchanges a refresh token for a new access token, without requiring the user to log in again.\n\nHow to use: send `{ \"refresh_token\": \"{{refresh_token}}\" }` — requires the variable to have been set by a previous `Login`.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` with a new `access_token`. `401 Unauthorized` if the refresh token is invalid, expired, or was revoked (e.g. after `Logout`).",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"refresh_token\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "description": "Revokes the current refresh token, ending the session server-side.\n\nHow to use: requires a valid Bearer `{{token}}`; send `{ \"userId\": string }` matching the logged-in user.\n\nWhat to expect: `200 OK` on success. After this, the previously issued `refresh_token` will be rejected by `Refresh Token`.",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"userId\": \"1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseURL}}/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseURL}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
